\subsection{Kelvin Grove Corridor}
\label{sec:network}

The Kelvin Grove corridor (Brisbane, Australia) is a 3.2\,km arterial segment
along Kelvin Grove Road comprising 12 coordinated signalised intersections
(\cref{fig:corridor}).  Bus route 345 operates with $\sim$10\,min
headways in mixed traffic; peak-hour flows reach 800--1200\,veh/h.  Each
intersection is instrumented with three detector classes per the corridor
configuration:

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item \textbf{Approach detectors} (\texttt{BusDet}): placed $\sim$40\,m
        upstream on the bus approach, triggering TSP evaluation when a bus
        crosses.
  \item \textbf{Exit detectors} (\texttt{BusExitDetectors}): placed $\sim$20\,m
        downstream of the stop-line, clearing the detection flag once the bus
        has passed.
  \item \textbf{Side-street detectors}: placed on cross-street approaches,
        measuring queue occupancy for spillback detection and cross-traffic
        delay estimation (Eq.\,\ref{eq:d_car}).
\end{itemize}

