\section{Appendix: Worked Timing Examples at One Intersection}
\label{sec:worked_examples}


Running example (junction 22603, Logan Road, measured plan): cycle $C = 80$\,s
with bus/main green $G_b = 53$\,s on $[0,53)$, intergreen $[53,57)$, side green
$G_s = 7$\,s on $[57,64)$ serving the 3804 side-street turnings, intergreen
$[64,68)$, other phases $[68,80)$.  A bus is due at $t = 50$ unless stated.
Each example gives the post-action intervals, who is blocked, the cycle
and offset effect on the progression overlap (\cref{eq:band_min}), and
whether the cycle can repay the debt this cycle.

\paragraph{GE$_{10}$ (bus present, green live).} Main runs to $63$; side is
pushed to $[67,74)$; $C = 90$, $\Delta\phi = +10$.  Blocked: the side approach
waits an extra $10$\,s plus its own queue discharge.  Recovery must trim
$10$\,s from upcoming phases, but the junction holds $\approx$0 headroom, so
the debt is unrecoverable and the $+10$ drift is permanent; downstream
arrivals shift $10$\,s toward red.  R8 prices the POG-weighted platoon loss
before the grant.

\paragraph{INS$_{10}$ (bus red, at $t = 70$).} A $10$\,s bus phase is inserted
at $[70,80)$, carved from the other-phase block, which loses $10$\,s (whatever
ran there is blocked $10$\,s).  $C = 90$, $\Delta\phi = +10$.  Admissible only
if the bus misses the natural green (reachability gate: arrival within about
one cycle); firing it minutes early disrupts the cross phase for a bus that
never comes.

\paragraph{ER$_{5}$ (bus already cleared at $t = 20$).} Main truncated to
$[0,20)$; the side advances $33$\,s early; $C = 75$, $\Delta\phi = -5$.
Blocked: nobody (the bus is past the stop line; the side gains).  Admissible
only on a cleared bus phase -- truncating with the bus still queued strands it
a full cycle.

\paragraph{GR$_{5}$.} Side shortened $[57,64) \to [57,59)$; the $5$\,s are
appended to the next main green; $C$ unchanged, $\Delta\phi = 0$.  Blocked:
$5$\,s of side green, absorbed by the side queue.  Cycle-neutral, hence exempt
from recovery: the cheapest way to advance a bus green.

\paragraph{OC$_{+5}$ (offset correction).} The whole plan shifts $+5$\,s;
$C$ unchanged.  Blocked: transiently everybody (each phase starts $5$\,s late
once).  Downstream absorbs the shift through the inbound mismatch terms
(the inbound mismatch terms) or the TWOWAY band vetoes it;
an OC that no neighbour can absorb just moves the mismatch downstream.

\paragraph{VP: skip the side (at $t = 57$).} Side gets $0$\,s; the controller
jumps to the next block; the cycle shortens by the skipped $11$\,s and the
offset advances.  Blocked: the entire side green ($7$\,s plus a full-cycle wait
for its queue).  Guards: skippable only with side queue below
$Q_{\max}^{\mathrm{skip}}$ and no consecutive skip under demand
(Eqs.\,\ref{eq:skip_queue}--\ref{eq:iam}).

\paragraph{PT: rotate side-first (next cycle).} Order becomes side--main: side
runs $[0,7)$, main starts $11$\,s late.  Blocked: the main platoon (delayed a
full side block) and every downstream arrival timed to the old offset.
Commits only if the predicted edge over the current sequence clears
$\Theta_{\mathrm{rot}}$; below it the order is
retained precisely because the offset disruption is not worth a marginal gain.

