\subsection{Method 0: Centralised Per-Second Phase Controller}
\label{sec:sol_centralised}
% ----------------------------------------------------

The centralised controller operates at a fixed 1\,Hz cadence, bypassing
bus-triggered detection entirely.  At each second, all 12 intersections are
evaluated simultaneously using Kalman-filtered bus position and flow estimates.

\noindent\textbf{Solves:} per junction per second, which of HOLD, TRANSITION,
or PHASE\_ROTATION maximises immediate corridor bus benefit minus
cross-street cost from the filtered state.  Myopic (no lookahead) and
unlearned: the same state always decides the same way.

\paragraph{Objective mapping (Type~D, not Type~A).} Centralised commits by its
own rule cascade (Alg.~\ref{alg:centralised}), not by the $Z_1$ layer: a myopic
per-second $Z_1$ approximation whose only exact-program quantity is the $Z_4$
veto (Fig.~\ref{fig:objectives}, rule-commit column).
The action space per intersection ($\approx$20 candidates per detection cycle) is:
\begin{center}
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{3.1cm}p{2.6cm}p{2.4cm}p{8.6cm}@{}}
\hline
Type & Action tokens & Durations & Description \\
\hline
No-op          & \texttt{NO\_ACTION}  & --              & Maintain current fixed-time schedule \\
Green Extension & \texttt{GE\_t}      & $t\in\{3,5,7,10,12,15\}$\,s & Extend the active green phase by $t$\,s \\
Phase Insertion & \texttt{INS\_t}     & $t\in\{10,12,15,20\}$\,s    & Insert a bus-priority phase of $t$\,s \\
Early Release (bus) & \texttt{ER\_BP\_t} & $t\in\{10,20,30\}$\,s   & Terminate the bus phase $t$\,s early \\
Early Release (ped) & \texttt{ER\_WP\_t} & $t\in\{10,20,30\}$\,s   & Terminate the waiting phase $t$\,s early \\
Green Reallocation (rotation of green) & \texttt{GR\_t} & $t\in\{5,10,15\}$\,s & Rotate $t$\,s of green from the donor phase to the bus phase (bus phase live only) \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\textbf{State.} Per intersection: current phase, elapsed time, Kalman-filtered
main and side flow rates ($\alpha = 0.3$ exponential smoothing), main-approach
queue length, count of approaching buses within 120\,s ETA window, and minimum
bus ETA via Kalman tracker.

\textbf{Decision logic.} At each tick each junction applies the per-second rule set of Alg.~\ref{alg:centralised} to its Kalman-filtered state ($\approx$20 candidates per junction; Kalman smoothing $\alpha = 0.3$ for the HOLD/TRANSITION flow comparison). The full rule cascade--HOLD/TRANSITION thresholds, two-step phase rotation, and the benefit-vs-cost comparisons--is stated executable-form in Alg.~\ref{alg:centralised}; the scored run then commits through Alg.~\ref{alg:master} lines 6--9.

